<title>FRANCE: Eurotunnel fire to cost Axa 100 mln Ffr.</title>
<headline>Eurotunnel fire to cost Axa 100 mln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The net cost to the merged Axa/UAP insurance group from December's fire in the Channel Tunnel will be more than 100 million francs ($18.5 million), chairman Claude Tendil said on Friday.</p>
<p>The gross cost, before re-insurance, is more than 500 million francs, he told a news conference.</p>
<p>UAP is lead insurer for tunnel operator Eurotunnel SA Plc for infrastructure damage and revenue losses. It said on November 26 its estimated maximum risk exposure was 75 million francs. ($ = 5.399 French Francs)</p>
</text>
